 "head": {
  "text": "WF-035 Synchronization rules: a glitch edge is used once"
 },
 "foot": {
  "text": "A one-clock dominant glitch inside the recessive bit is a recessive to dominant edge after a recessive sample: it resynchronizes once (rule 2). A second edge before the next sample point is ignored (rule 1), and a dominant to recessive edge never synchronizes (rule 4)."
 }
